                    <note type="editorial">
    
  
   See the discussions in <persName key="SHE01">Shelley</persName> and <persName key="PER03">Percy</persName><p> From 1827 Percy has been consistently coded as <persName key="SHE03">Percy Shelley jr</persName>, who is eight in the November of that year.
   There are good grounds for thinking that from this point
    on (around 100 references 1827-36) Godwin uses Percy to refer to his grandson. On many occasions Percy appears with <persName key="SHE02"> Mary Wollstonecraft Shelley</persName>
    and we know that  'Percy to Slater' (27 March 1828) refers to Percy junr entering
    Edward Slater's Gentlemen's Academy, Church Street, Kensington. </p></note>
